    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** offense is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest daily efficiency score of 83.29. He faces Matthews in an ideal scenario: a favorable SP_xERA of 4.32, a primary leadoff spot, and a high-probability SB environment facilitated by the pitcher's slow delivery. We are also capitalizing on the high floor of **Drake Baldwin** (68.18) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (65.89). **Drake Baldwin** is particularly well-positioned as he benefits from a weak 4.62 xERA opposing starter and a premier #2 lineup spot, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** maintains a high base projection despite facing a tougher arm in Suarez, buoyed by a significant dynamic platoon advantage.\n\nDeciding between our outfield depth and middle infield options required careful calibration, particularly regarding SB upside. **Nasim Nunez** (54.33) remains in the lineup despite a suboptimal #9 spot because his speed is critical for our 5x5 objectives; however, **Andy Pages** (58.24) and **Kyle Tucker** (63.95) represent our most difficult bench decisions. **Andy Pages** narrowly missed the primary starting slots despite strong projections, as his utility value is currently overshadowed by the platoon-specific advantages of **Sam Antonacci** (63.14). While **Coby Mayo** was analyzed, he remains benched due to a lack of confirmed playing time, leaving our current rotation to focus on high-efficiency, full-game starters.\n\nWe are monitoring several situational risks as we set today\u2019s roster. **Kyle Tucker** and **Wade Meckler** are both operating under \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions; should their actual batting orders drop significantly, their effectiveness\u2014and by extension our 5x5 totals\u2014could fluctuate. Additionally, while **Luis Robert Jr.** (51.27) and **Heliot Ramos** (46.67) are active, they face a challenging matchup against Miller, B, whose 3.42 xERA necessitates a conservative outlook on their individual performance ceilings. We will continue to monitor the status of injured assets like **Jordan Westburg** and **Josh Jung**, but for today, the core remains committed to **Gunnar Henderson** and the high-upside production of our top-tier starters.",
